  ('TL1-35','Cave',1,'Tongariro','2024, Version 9','Scope Training and Assessment Path With this competency, the instructor is able to lead trips in Observation simple horizontal caves with site specific sign-off. Can be done by a Developing Instructor step 2. Sites within the scope may include: Assessment ✓ Pukehinau Cave Assessor must be an Outdoor Instructor step 2 and hold ✓ Okupata Cave Cave (L1) with Training department approval ✓ Walk down Dry Valley and up the Pukehinau Stream Assessment is by direct observation and site specific The instructor may only operate unsupervised at sites that have been approved. Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current ❑ L1 Communication Competence ❑ Complete site induction of a round trip of Okupata Cave: main entrance, knee deep pool, escape route to upper entrance. • NZOIA Cave 1 • 5 personal and 5 Logged Instruction days + Observation and local famil A Site: ........................ O b s 1 O b s 2 S elf ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate personal competence in a cave.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1),
  ('TL1-37','High Ropes Course',1,'Tongariro','2024, version 9','Scope Training and Assessment Path This competency is for those operating all basic elements of the Hillary Observation can be done by an Outdoor Outdoors High Ropes. Instructor. NB: There is a specific L2 Competency for the Trapeze and the Big Swing and above ground rescues. The instructor must be on direct Assessor must be a Senior Instructor with supervision for these elements until assessed as competent Training department approval Assessment is by direct observation Prerequisites Recorded Recognition of Current • Knowledge and relevant experience of current standard practice in Competence New Zealand ropes skills. All Require site famil • High Ropes Certificate • NZOIA Rock Leader + famil 2 ropes only • NZOIA rock 1 • 10 Logged Instruction days in HR + observe and famils • Some RCC From Rock Climbing (L1) A O b s 1 O b s 2 s elf ssesso r Technical Competence 1. Demonstrate and describe the care and appropriate use of HR gear and equipment.','{"self": "Self", "obs1": "Obs 1", "obs2": "Obs 2", "assess1": "Assessor"}',1),
