  ('TL4-15',20,'Technical Competence',null,'1. Demonstrate an understanding of contemporary issues affecting whitewater kayaking The candidate will have an understanding and awareness of:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',30,'Technical Competence',null,'• Current threats to New Zealand’s rivers and the effect these have on recreational river use',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',40,'Technical Competence',null,'• Legislation relevant to recreational kayaking',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',50,'Technical Competence',null,'2. Demonstrate the care and correct use of kayaking gear and equipment commonly used in New Zealand The candidate will:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',60,'Technical Competence',null,'• Have knowledge about equipment commonly used in New Zealand, including the types, characteristics, advantages, limitations, cost, care, maintenance and storage for a range of equipment e.g. kayaks, PFD’s, spray decks, paddles, helmets, dry tops/ paddle jac kets and other clothing and footwear suitable for kayaking',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',70,'Technical Competence',null,'• Role model the use of gear and equipment that is in good condition, well maintained and wear clothing and footwear that is appropriate for use in a class 3 whitewater environment',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',80,'Technical Competence',null,'• Demonstrate safe transportation of kayaks on trailers and / or roof racks',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',90,'Technical Competence',null,'• Demonstrate a working knowledge of a range of safety equipment e.g. buoyancy bags, survival bags, tow-lines, throw-bags, slings, karabiners, Prusiks, knife, saw, split paddle, pulleys and dynamic/static ropes',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',100,'Technical Competence',null,'• The candidate will demonstrate a working knowledge of a range of knots applicable to kayaking e.g. truckers hitch, round turn and two half hitches, clove hitch, bowline, figure eight, Italian hitch, Prusik knots',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',110,'Technical Competence',null,'• Be able to impart knowledge to intermediate/advanced level kayakers about kayaks, clothing and equipment appropriate for use on class 3 whitewater',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',120,'Technical Competence',null,'3. Demonstrate river rescue skills The candidate will demonstrate the following river rescue skills at a given location on a class 3 river section:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',130,'Technical Competence',null,'• Instructor assist and instructor intervention rescues: - Two of the following three rescues: Bow (or T) Rescue, H Assist, Barrel Roll - Transport a swimmer across the river using a bow carry or a stern deck carry and a tow - Deep water rescue Recommended time for kayak emptied, kayaker back in and spray deck on is 2 minutes',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',140,'Technical Competence',null,'• Use and knowledge of an effective towline system: - Capsize, release and roll - Assisted ferry glide - Towing – a kayak and a paddle - Rescue of an unconscious swimmer',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',150,'Technical Competence',null,'• Rescue a swimmer using a throw bag to rescue a swimmer - attention gained, accurate throw, stable belay, safe pendulum, re-throw coils 10m',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',160,'Technical Competence',null,'• A recovery system for a stranded/trapped kayaker • A recovery system for a pinned kayak using pulley/mechanical advantage systems and show an understanding of the limitations and dangers of these systems (For assessment efficiency this can be done as a simulated rescue on land)',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',170,'Technical Competence',null,'• Using an improvised harness to ascend/descend a rope with standard river rescue equipment',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',180,'Technical Competence',null,'• A working knowledge of management strategies for a given river rescue scenario',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',190,'Technical Competence',null,'4. Demonstrate personal kayaking skills on class 3 and class 4 whitewater The candidate will demonstrate kayaking on class 4 including:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',200,'Technical Competence',null,'• A reliable roll',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',210,'Technical Competence',null,'• Controlled river running',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',220,'Technical Competence',null,'The candidate will demonstrate the following role model kayaking skills (i.e. making good visual images suitable for students to learn from) on class 3:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',230,'Technical Competence',null,'• A range of efficient and effective paddling techniques e.g. forward, reverse and sweep strokes, bracing, edging/railing, sweep to stern draws, gliding draws, body position and rotation',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',240,'Technical Competence',null,'• A role model kayak roll on both sides',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',250,'Technical Competence',null,'• A variety of different turns e.g. carve, skid, pivot',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',260,'Technical Competence',null,'• Forward and reverse ferry gliding',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',270,'Technical Competence',null,'• Safe and efficient river running and river moves including choosing lines /routes down rapids',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',280,'The Environment',null,'5. Role model accepted environmental practices',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',290,'The Environment',null,'• Demonstrate and/or describe the responsibilities to land owners, including access protocols and issues, and other river users',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',300,'The Environment',null,'• Demonstrate minimal impact practices at all times',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',310,'The Environment',null,'• Role model the principles of the New Zealand Water Care Code, the New Zealand Environmental Care Code and/or Leave No Trace',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',320,'The Environment',null,'• Demonstrate an awareness of practices to stop the spread of Didymo and other freshwater pests',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',330,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'6. Lead and manage a group on class 3 whitewater The candidate will demonstrate competent leadership and management of a group on class 3 whitewater which includes:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',340,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Awareness and disclosure of relevant hazards encountered and suitable management techniques',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',350,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• A range of on the water group management strategies as appropriate',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',360,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Effective and proactive management of the group including; anticipation of capsizes, dealing with differences in abilities of party members, protecting rapids as appropriate',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',370,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• An effective communication system for managing the group',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',380,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Establishing rapport and using a leadership style appropriate to the group',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',390,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Organise and motivate a group / individuals in a whitewater environment',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',400,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'7. Apply effective safety management. The candidate will demonstrate the following:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',410,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• The ability to access and apply weather and up-to-date river information (including river flow) as appropriate for a planned session or river trip',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',420,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Have a first aid kit and be able to deal with first aid situations as required',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',430,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Awareness of the risks and appropriate risk management strategies during a given river trip and the ability to adjust plans when required',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',440,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Awareness of the prevention, symptoms, remedies and treatment for common medical issues relevant to kayaking e.g. near drowning, hypothermia, shock, sunburn, dehydration, shoulder dislocation',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',450,'Group Management and Leadership',null,'• Safe practices and good judgement and decision making within the scope of this qualification',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',460,'Instruction',null,'8. Teach moving water skills in preparation for a class 3 river trip. The candidate will demonstrate teaching on class 1 or 2 whitewater, including:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',470,'Instruction',null,'• Selecting a suitable training site',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',480,'Instruction',null,'• Providing a safe, well managed and positive learning experience',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',490,'Instruction',null,'• Teaching kayaking skills that prepare students for a class 3 river trip',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',500,'Instruction',null,'9. Teach river running skills on a class 3 river trip The candidate will demonstrate teaching river running skills on a class 3 river trip, including:',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',510,'Instruction',null,'• Selecting a suitable river trip',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',520,'Instruction',null,'• Identifying river features and hazards and how to use and/or avoid them',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',530,'Instruction',null,'• Effective communication including the use of paddle signals, voice and whistle',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',540,'Instruction',null,'• River running strategies, including scouting and choosing safe lines through rapids',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',550,'Instruction',null,'• Teaching kayaking skills to enhance students’ ability to paddle class 3 whit ewater',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-15',560,'Instruction',null,'• Providing a safe, well managed and positive learning experience',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',10,'SMS',null,'Managed within the T1, T2 and T3 requirements',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',20,'Technical Competence','1. Describe alpine climbing history and an awareness of:',' The development of alpine climbing as a sport and current developments and trends',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',30,'Technical Competence','2. Demonstrate the care and correct use of alpine climbing equipment',' Role model the use of gear and equipment that is in good condition, well maintained and is used in accordance with the manufacturer’s recommendations and current best practice',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',40,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate technical mountaineering skills','• Lead climbing on snow/ice to 70 0',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',50,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate technical mountaineering skills','• Ridge travel to show rope management e.g. moving together, short pitches for awkward section',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',60,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate technical mountaineering skills','• The use of short roping to safeguard a client',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',70,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate technical mountaineering skills','• The construction of anchors suitable to the conditions : o Rock anchors e.g. wires, stoppers, hexes, camming devices o Snow anchors e.g. vertical snow stake, snow pig, mid-clip, T-slot, snow bollard o Ice anchors e.g. ice screws, ice bollard, V-thread',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',80,'Technical Competence','3. Demonstrate technical mountaineering skills','• Safe and efficient belay methods suitable for the application they are being used: o Describing the advantages and disadvantages of a variety of belay methods and their suitability for managing leaders and/or seconds e.g. Italian hitch, manual locking belay device, standing ice axe belay (Austrian or Stomper), waist/shoulder belay, direct belay o Clear communication and systematic checks',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',90,'Technical Competence','4. Construct a top tope climbing system','• Use of a personal safety system while exposed to a potential fall during setup (lead climb up or top access)',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',100,'Technical Competence','5. Demonstrate and apply knowledge of glaciated terrain skills','• Be able to describe glacier processes and identify landforms associated with glaciation',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',110,'Technical Competence','5. Demonstrate and apply knowledge of glaciated terrain skills','• Describe the hazards associated with glaciated terrain and considerations for selecting a safe route through glaciated terrain',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',120,'Technical Competence','5. Demonstrate and apply knowledge of glaciated terrain skills','• Demonstrate roping up for glacier travel',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',130,'Technical Competence','5. Demonstrate and apply knowledge of glaciated terrain skills','• Demonstrate crevasse rescue: o Hold a fall; build anchor, transfer load to the anchor and escape the system, construct hauling system, preparing lip as required, haul with assistance from victim and turn this into an unassisted haul for an unconscious victim.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',140,'Technical Competence','6. Demonstrate avalanche and snow safety skills','• Demonstrate making route selection and activity location choices that fit with the weather and avalanche hazard forecast and minimise exposure to avalanches',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',150,'Technical Competence','6. Demonstrate avalanche and snow safety skills','• Be able to demonstrate any skills or knowledge contained within the Avalanche Risk Management Stage 1 qualification',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',160,'The Environment','7. Demonstrate knowledge of meteorology and apply weather interpretation and forecasting skills','• Be able to describe global weather systems and global influences on New Zealand’s weather e.g. Coriolis Effect, Hadley Cells, El Niño, La Niña',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',170,'The Environment','8. Demonstrate and/or describe cultural and environmental knowledge of the NZ alpine environment','• Demonstrate a broad knowledge of the flora, fauna, geology and history of the New Zealand’s alpine regions',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',180,'The Environment','8. Demonstrate and/or describe cultural and environmental knowledge of the NZ alpine environment','• Have significant knowledge of and be able to describe the history and purpose of the major organisations involved in the administration, protection and advocacy of New Zealand’s alpine environments e.g. DOC, NZ Alpine Club, Federated Mountain Clubs, Mountain Safety Council, Forest and Bird',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',190,'Group Management and Leadership','9. Apply effective safety management','• Manage participants’ safety by appropriate; route and site selection, and equipment use and checks as required',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',200,'Group Management and Leadership','9. Apply effective safety management','• Demonstrate assessing climbing routes for hazards and demonstrate risk management principles to minimize or avoid the impact of any identified hazards',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',210,'Group Management and Leadership','9. Apply effective safety management','• Demonstrate safe practices and good judgment and decision-making within the scope of this qualification [trip 1]',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',220,'Group Management and Leadership','9. Apply effective safety management','• Demonstrate safe practices and good judgment and decision-making within the scope of this qualification [trip 2]',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',230,'Group Management and Leadership','9. Apply effective safety management','• Never compromise their personal safety or the safety of their participants',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',240,'Group Management and Leadership','10. Lead and manage participants during alpine climbing','• Supervising and coaching climbers and belayers',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',250,'Group Management and Leadership','10. Lead and manage participants during alpine climbing','• A leadership style that is appropriate for the participants; their skill and experience level and their needs',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',260,'Group Management and Leadership','10. Lead and manage participants during alpine climbing','• Manage participants safely and effectively both climbing and descending',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',270,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','• Use of terrain and route-selection',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',280,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','• Snow, Ice and Rock movement skills',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',290,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','• Placing protection for multi-pitch lead climbing',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',300,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','• Efficient and safe belaying of a lead climber including clear communication between belayer and climber',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',310,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','• Climbing and descending a multi-pitch route',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',320,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','• Ice and mixed climbing techniques',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',330,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','The candidate will use: A logical sequence of teaching progressions',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',340,'Instruction','11. Instruct safe and well managed and positive learning experiences for participants','Clear demonstrations and explanations',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',350,'Instruction','12. Prepare and deliver teaching sessions','• The candidate will prepare and deliver teaching sessions on any topics or skills contained in this L4 competency which may include, but is not limited to - anchor building, snow safety and avalanche rescue, glaciated terrain travel and crevasse rescue, ice and mixed climbing techniques.',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',360,'Instruction','12. Prepare and deliver teaching sessions','• A range of teaching skills e.g. introduction, appropriate voice, language and body language, teaching/visual aids, demonstrations, use of teachable moments, evaluation of learning',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',370,'Instruction','12. Prepare and deliver teaching sessions','• A wide knowledge of the topics and skills',true,true,true,true,false,false),
  ('TL4-19',380,'Instruction','12. Prepare and deliver teaching sessions','• Creating a positive learning environment which encourages enthusiasm, interest and learning',true,true,true,true,false,false),
